763
00:39:34,740 --> 00:39:39,620
So in this lecture, we have focused on facility design,

764
00:39:39,620 --> 00:39:43,640
directional airflow, and biological safety cabinets.

765
00:39:43,640 --> 00:39:45,260
As I mentioned earlier,

766
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:50,280
design of the facility involves analysis of the site

767
00:39:51,660 --> 00:39:54,440
and your facility should ideally be located

768
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:57,620
in a place where there is low incidence

769
00:39:57,620 --> 00:40:01,020
of natural disasters and away from populated areas.

770
00:40:01,020 --> 00:40:04,420
The basic facility design comprises three floors.

771
00:40:04,420 --> 00:40:08,900
So we have two service floors and the laboratory itself.

772
00:40:08,900 --> 00:40:10,780
So this is your laboratory floor.

773
00:40:10,780 --> 00:40:13,300
You have your BSL laboratory here.

774
00:40:13,300 --> 00:40:15,940
This is your air handling units.

775
00:40:15,940 --> 00:40:20,780
And this is your waste disposal system

776
00:40:20,780 --> 00:40:24,580
or the EDS, effluent disposal system.

777
00:40:24,580 --> 00:40:27,340
This is the basic design of a facility.

778
00:40:28,540 --> 00:40:34,240
And finally, we have looked at biological safety cabinets.

779
